From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gma500: Count Cedarview vblanks in FRAMEHIGH alone

gma_crtc_get_vblank_counter() builds the count as FRAMEHIGH << 8 |
the frame byte of FRAMEPIXEL. On Cedarview that byte stays 0 and
FRAMEHIGH alone counts frames, one a vblank (pipe B of an Atom N2600),
so the DRM vblank count advanced by 256 a vblank. Clients pacing with
it (GLX_OML_sync_control's MSC, glXSwapBuffersMscOML) saw every frame
as 255 vblanks late and ran unpaced.

On Cedarview, count FRAMEHIGH's 16 bits and say so in
max_vblank_count.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/psb_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/psb_drv.c
@@ -396,7 +396,8 @@ static int psb_driver_load(struct drm_device *dev, unsigned long flags)
 	if (dev_priv->ops->sgx)
 		gma_sgx_aux_init(dev);
 
-	dev->max_vblank_count = 0xffffff; /* only 24 bits of frame count */
+	/* 24 bits of frame count; Cedarview counts in FRAMEHIGH's 16 alone */
+	dev->max_vblank_count = IS_CDV(dev) ? 0xffff : 0xffffff;
 
 	psb_modeset_init(dev);
 	drm_kms_helper_poll_init(dev);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/psb_irq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/psb_irq.c
@@ -497,7 +497,15 @@ u32 gma_crtc_get_vblank_counter(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 			 PIPE_FRAME_HIGH_SHIFT);
 	} while (high1 != high2);
 
-	count = (high1 << 8) | low;
+	/*
+	 * Cedarview's frame counter is FRAMEHIGH alone, a frame a count; its
+	 * FRAMEPIXEL frame byte stays 0, so the high << 8 | low count of the
+	 * others advanced 256 a vblank there.
+	 */
+	if (IS_CDV(dev))
+		count = high1;
+	else
+		count = (high1 << 8) | low;
 
 err_gma_power_end:
 	gma_power_end(dev);
